      ":question/math-academy-id": "e-380",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int -6(7^x) \\, \\textrm d x.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we factor out the constant $-6.$ Then, we integrate the exponential function, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int (-6)7^x  \\, \\textrm d x   \n&= -6\\int 7^x\\,\\textrm{d}x\\\\\n&=-6 \\cdot \\dfrac{7^x}{\\ln 7} + C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
